- Meet session browse's <200 ms warm-start target. Universal CLI imports and
  SQLAlchemy-backed index loading dominate; keep one command registration and read
  path instead of adding a parallel fast CLI loader.
- In `cli/spawn.py:_spawn_list`, the `--all` shortcut silently drops the default
  `limit` from 20 to 5 (`if limit == 20: limit = 5`). The hint printed by
  `work show` therefore uses `--view all --limit N`, where `N` is the total number
  of associated spawns: `--view all` reserves slots for active rows, so a limit
  equal to the finished count drops finished rows. Either make `--all` mean all or
  document the cap, then simplify the hint.
- In 0.29.0, end the deprecation of `meridian spawn message`: it fails with one line that
  names `meridian message`, as the 0.28.0 changelog and `docs/upgrading.md` promise. Its
  handler in `cli/spawn.py` stops calling `run_message` and loses the stderr deprecation
  line, and `SANDBOX_BLOCKED_SENTENCE` (`lib/core/caller_boundary.py`) loses its
  `meridian spawn message` clause.
